Subject: [PATCH] media: hi556: expose orientation and rotation from the fwnode

libcamera treats V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION as a requirement and says so
plainly when it is missing:

  'hi556 3-0020': Recommended V4L2 control 0x009a0922 not supported
  'hi556 3-0020': The sensor kernel driver needs to be fixed
  'hi556 3-0020': Failed to retrieve the camera location

Parse the standard "orientation" and "rotation" device-tree properties and
create the corresponding controls, the same way ov5675 already does.

Both properties are optional in the fwnode helper: one that is absent creates
no control, so this does not become a new requirement on device trees that do
not carry them.

The controls are read-only, so __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() skips them and
hi556_set_ctrl()'s default -EINVAL case is never reached for them --
verified against the skip in __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup().

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
@@ -815,12 +815,14 @@
 
 static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 {
+	struct v4l2_fwnode_device_properties props;
+	struct i2c_client *client = v4l2_get_subdevdata(&hi556->sd);
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler *ctrl_hdlr;
 	s64 exposure_max, h_blank;
 	int ret;
 
 	ctrl_hdlr = &hi556->ctrl_handler;
-	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 8);
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(ctrl_hdlr, 10);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -874,6 +876,30 @@
 	if (ctrl_hdlr->error)
 		return ctrl_hdlr->error;
 
+	/*
+	 * V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION and V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION,
+	 * from the "orientation" and "rotation" device-tree properties.
+	 * libcamera treats the first as a requirement and says so:
+	 *
+	 *   'hi556 3-0020': Recommended V4L2 control 0x009a0922 not supported
+	 *   'hi556 3-0020': The sensor kernel driver needs to be fixed
+	 *
+	 * Both are optional in the fwnode helper: a property that is absent
+	 * simply creates no control, so this does not become a requirement on
+	 * device trees that do not carry them.
+	 */
+	ret = v4l2_fwnode_device_parse(&client->dev, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(ctrl_hdlr, &hi556_ctrl_ops,
+					      &props);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (ctrl_hdlr->error)
+		return ctrl_hdlr->error;
+
 	hi556->sd.ctrl_handler = ctrl_hdlr;
 
 	return 0;
